\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\tab God is the refuge of His saints,
\par \pard\li720 When storms of sharp distress invade ;
\par Ere we can offer our complaints,
\par Behold Him present with His aid !
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.\tab let mountains from their seats be hurled
\par \pard\li720 sown to the deep, and buried there,
\par convulsions shake the solid world,
\par our faith shall never yield to fear.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.\tab Loud may the troubled ocean roar ;
\par \pard\li720 In sacred peace our souls abide ;
\par While every nation, every shore,
\par Trembles, and dreads the swelling tide.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.\tab There is a stream, whose gentle flow
\par \pard\fi360\li360 makes glad the city of our God,
\par life, love, and joy still gliding through,
\par and watering our divine abode.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.\tab This sacred stream, Thy vital word,
\par \pard\li720 Thus all our raging fear controls ;
\par Sweet peace Thy promises afford,
\par And give new strength to fainting souls.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.\tab Zion enjoys her Monarch's love,
\par \pard\li720 Secure against the threatening hour ;
\par Nor can her firm foundation move,
\par Built on His faithfulness and power.
\par \pard 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

